{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2961","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2961","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2961\",\"parent_revision\":\"a4c28807dd2e6abb37a40b39015c8648324e1345dfa1ec0223a8d7587937d897\",\"root_revision\":\"a4c28807dd2e6abb37a40b39015c8648324e1345dfa1ec0223a8d7587937d897\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/analyze.md`'s Discovery Gate can invoke the full `dh:discovery` skill (which runs its own investigation into the item's technology/domain) before reaching `swarm.md`. `swarm.md`'s Wave 0 independently spawns `technical-researcher`, which runs four research angles (api-state, ecosystem-research, impact-measurement, codebase-auditor) over the same item's same technology and concern.\\n\\nOn #2953, by the time Wave 0 would have run, the discovery-gate investigation had already produced answers to essentially the same questions Wave 0's four-angle research would ask (PyGithub API state, ecosystem feasibility of candidate libraries, codebase audit of the target module and its tests). Nothing in either workflow file flags this overlap or instructs the orchestrator to reuse the discovery artifact's findings instead of re-running Wave 0's full research pass. Left to run both as documented, this item's grooming would have spawned a second full multi-angle research pass over nearly identical ground the discovery gate just covered \u2014 doubling agent cost and wall-clock time for redundant findings, with no mechanism in the documented workflow to detect or prevent it.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 discovered live while grooming #2953 via /dh:work-backlog-item, 2026-08-18\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **groom's discovery-gate investigation (analyze.md) and swarm's wave 0 technical-researcher cover overlapping research ground with no deduplication** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f0cfc61ddf4d607e480b10265326f9038536ada07072290f15d2a097a2739791\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTpDIQ\"}"}